      "problem": "If $\\overline{P} = \\{ 2, 4, 6 \\}$ and $\\overline{Q} = \\{ 1, 2, 4 \\},$ then what is $\\overline{ P \\cap Q }?$",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for intersections states that\n\n$$\n\\overline{P \\cap Q} \\equiv \\overline{P} \\cup \\overline{Q}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{P\\cap Q} & =\\overset{―}{P}\\cup \\overset{―}{Q} \\\\  & =\\{2,4,6\\}\\cup \\{1,2,4\\} \\\\  & =\\{1,2,4,6\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
